<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 205 0 R
/E (Visual and hands-on representations make abstract computational concepts more accessible for students with language barriers, lower reading levels, or special educational needs. By combining visual materials, demonstrations, and physical interaction with robots, teachers created a learning environment where students could understand programming concepts through observation and experimentation. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
870 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 205 0 R
/E (This practice can easily be transferred to other educational contexts because it relies on simple strategies such as visual aids, demonstrations, and step-by-step modelling. Teachers can adapt the approach using materials already available in classrooms, including printed command cards, floor maps, storyboards, or diagrams.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
